# A computed declaration is code executed at its line (the author 2026-11-11, R12; plan M11 5a): run over itself,
# Computed gives x its value at the line `int: x five()`, the read below that line sees 5, and the place is published
# into the slot of the declaration at the end of the launch.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
fn: five () int
    return: 5
sub: main () (
    Computed:
        int: x five()
        int: y
        y := x + 1
)
    call: Computed
main()
int: seen main\data\Computed\y
int: published main\data\Computed\x
